  <Vertical id="wj1_orientations">
  <Markdown>
## The Circle's Shorthand: Writer Orientations

The writer's circle has seen a lot of different writers and noticed that they tend to fall into general
types. They've developed shorthand to name the writer types they've noticed.

| | Orientation | In their words |
|---|---|---|
| 🤝 | **Community writer** *(Alma)* | "Almost everything I write is pointed at another person." |
| 🧭 | **Explorer** *(Lee)* | "I write to find out what I think about things." |
| 🔧 | **Technician** *(Richard)* | "I write so things get done properly the first time." |

Nobody hands you one of these. At the end of the session you'll read through the whole deck and **pick the
one that sounds most like you** — and then, as Richard puts it, *say what makes you sure. That's the
useful part.*

Those three are just the ones Alma, Lee, and Richard use. **There are eight writer types in all**, and at
the end the deck is yours to browse and choose from — with a **blank card** at the back if none of the
eight is you:

| | Writer type | In a nutshell |
|---|---|---|
| 🤝 | **Community Writer** | Writes to connect with people *(Alma)* |
| 🧭 | **Explorer** | Writes to find out what they think *(Lee)* |
| 🔧 | **Technician** | Writes to get things done clearly and correctly *(Richard)* |
| 🌿 | **Hobbyist** | Writes for the enjoyment of it |
| 💭 | **Dreamer** | Writes to express an inner life |
| 🔁 | **Practitioner** | Writes steadily, as a practical habit |
| 🏁 | **Finisher** | Writes to finish something real |
| 🎯 | **Pragmatist** | Writes to reach and affect an audience |
  </Markdown>
  <Done id="wj1_orientations_done" label="Mark as read" />
  </Vertical>

