  <Vertical id="wj1_why">
    <Markdown>
## Why I Write

Here's the thing a board can't tell you. Two people can write the exact same grocery list — one to get
the shopping done, one because it quiets a busy mind. Same item, completely different activity. *It only
looks the same from outside.*

So go back through your writing and put the **why** on it. For each group below, pick the reason that fits
best. There's no right answer — pick what's true for **you.**
    </Markdown>

    <Collapsible id="wj1_why_board_reminder" title="Remind me what's on my board">
      <Markdown>*Here's the board you built — most often at the top. You can even nudge it here if you left something out.*</Markdown>
      <Markdown>**🏫 For school:**</Markdown>
      <Use ref="wj1_board_school" />
      <Markdown>**🌙 Outside school:**</Markdown>
      <Use ref="wj1_board_outside" />
    </Collapsible>

    <Markdown>### 💬 Messaging &amp; staying in touch *(texts, DMs, group chats)*</Markdown>
    <DropdownInput id="wj1_why_messaging" placeholder="Mostly, I do this…">
      I don't really do this sort of writing    | dont_do
      To stay in touch with people I care about | stay_in_touch
      To be part of a group or community        | community
      To figure out what I think                | figure_out
      To try something out and see what happens | try_out
      To get something done or stay organized   | get_done
      To remember something                     | remember
      To make something I'm proud of            | proud
      Because I enjoy it                        | enjoy
      To work out how I'm feeling               | feelings
      To persuade someone or make a point       | persuade
      Because a class or a job requires it      | required
      Something else (I'll describe it below)   | something_else
    </DropdownInput>
